Which of the following statements is the most incorrect?

public class MyCustomTagHandler extends SimpleTagSupport {
    private String message;

    public void setMessage(String message) {
        this.message = message;
    }

    public void doTag() throws JspException, IOException {
        JspWriter out = getJspContext().getOut();
        out.println(message);
    }
}

How would you use this custom tag in a JSP page?

You are developing a JSP application that requires user authentication. Explain how you would use session management to track the user's login status and securely store user information.

<%@ page import="javax.servlet.http.HttpSession" %>
<%
HttpSession session = request.getSession();
session.setAttribute("loggedInUser", "username");
%>

JavaScript clients of SignalR application call public methods on hubs via the invoke method of the HubConnection. The invoke method accepts the name of the hub method and any arguments defined in the hub method.

Suppose that you already have defined the following code:

var connection = new signalR.HubConnectionBuilder()
    .withUrl("/chatHub")
    .create();

connection.start();

Which of the following codes can call the "invoke" method?

try {
    await connection.invoke("SendMessage", user, message);
} catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
}

try {
    await connection.invoke(user, message, "SendMessage");
} catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
}

